    "title": "Agent ran a destructive git or filesystem action",
    "desc": "An agent account did something destructive or history-rewriting - a force push, a branch delete, a reflog expiry or filter-repo (destroying the record of what it committed), a hard reset far back, `git clean -fdx`, an `rm -rf` of a repo or home, or a database drop. Empirically this is the most common real agent harm: agents deleting repos, branches and data. For a human, force-push is routine; for the agent it should be a reviewed event, and `reflog expire --expire=now` + `gc --prune=now` is covering tracks inside git itself. Worker branches (squashed before a PR, which is sanctioned) are carved out.",
